    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-050 — `@supports` conditional rules.** Two commits pushed. **Third commit (docs) follows after merge.**\n\nCloses a gap that has existed since the CSS parser was first vendored: every `@supports` block was silently dropped. **73 blocks in Wikipedia CSS** now reach the cascade.\n\n## The decisive proof\n\nLayout verification on the real Wikipedia HTML article:\n\n```\n.vector-pinned-container computed style:\n  display = block         ← was none (from top-level rule only)\n```\n\n**That rule only exists inside `@supports (display: grid)`.** Pre-ADR-050, the `@supports` block was dropped entirely, so `.vector-pinned-container` fell back to the top-level `display: none`. Now it's `display: block` — the `@supports` gate fired, the block's rules entered cascade, and the later-source-order rule won over `display: none`.\n\n## What shipped (Commits 1 + 2)\n\n### Commit 1 — `@supports` parse + evaluator (`a10c97d`)\n\n- `supported_properties()` — set of properties the engine parses\n- `supported_pseudos()` — ADR-018 + ADR-038 pseudo set\n- `unsupported_value()` — rejects `round`/`sqrt`/`sin`/`cos`/`tan` (ADR-037 deferral) and `dotted`/`dashed` (ADR-040 deferral)\n- `feature_query_supported()` — recursive evaluator for `not` / `or` / `and` / `selector(...)` / `(prop: value)`\n- `parse_supports_block()` — top-level + `@media`-nested\n- Top-level `@supports` sibling branch to `@media` in `parse()`\n- `@media`-nested `@supports` recursive parse (replaces `skip_at_rule` for `@supports` only)\n\n**Critical evaluator fix during implementation**: initial outer-paren-stripped branch called `feature_query_single(inner)` instead of recursing. That made `not ((A) or (B))` return `not(false) = true` when both A and B were supported — which would have wrongly included the `@supports not (mask-image)` fallback block, producing **double-rendered icons** with ADR-047's mask rules. Fixed by recursing: `not ((mask-image) or (-webkit-mask-image))` now correctly returns `false` when both are supported.\n\n### Commit 2 — 15 unit tests (`fb20870`)\n\n- `(display: grid)` includes, `(display: block)` includes\n- `(width: round(...))` drops, `not (width: round(...))` includes\n- `(mask-image: none)` includes, `not (mask-image: none)` drops\n- `(A) or (B)` mask includes\n- **`not ((A) or (B))` mask case drops — the load-bearing test** (no double-rendered icons)\n- `(text-decoration: underline dotted)` drops\n- `not selector(:focus-visible)` includes\n- `selector(:hover)` includes\n- `@media { @supports }` propagates MediaQuery\n- Empty body, malformed prelude, multiple declarations\n\n**Test count: 611 → 626 cases, 2386 → 2407 assertions.**\n\n## Honest delta framing\n\n**Verified at layout-tree level**: `.vector-pinned-container` display: none → block. The rule reaches cascade, which is the ADR-050 mechanism working.\n\n**Not yet verified at first-viewport PNG**: whether the sidebar TOC visually renders. Other culling rules in `.vector-main-menu-landmark` / `.vector-column-start` ancestors may still block it. Documented in ADR-050's acceptance criteria as: \"PNG verification (visible sidebar delta or documented zero-delta with layout-tree proof)\".\n\n**Same category as ADR-045** (scroll-PNG verified when the target renders) or ADR-047/048 (behaviorally-complete, no consumer) depending on the PNG check.\n\n## Rules-parsed count note\n\nPost-ADR-050, rules parsed total: **968**. Prior \"~1147\" was an unreliable guess (never cleanly measured this session). `display = block` on the pinned-container is a per-element proof that's stronger than any aggregate count: without ADR-050, that rule could never reach the cascade.\n\n## Commits\n\n| # | SHA | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `a10c97d` | `@supports` parse + evaluator |\n| 2 | `fb20870` | 15 unit tests |\n| 3 | (post-merge) | docs: ADR-050 → Implemented, Post-ADR-050 note in ADR-027 |\n\nRefs #231\n",
